# Protocol-X Tool MCP — environment configuration example
# Copy to .env (or export) — every key is optional; defaults shown.

# --- Core server ---
# Data directory: protox.db (SQLite), audit.jsonl, logs
# PROTOX_DATA_DIR=~/.local/share/protocol-x
# Workspace root: all tool file I/O is confined here (INV-5)
# PROTOX_WORKSPACE=~/.local/share/protocol-x/workspace
# HTTP bind (Streamable HTTP transport + console)
# PROTOX_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PROTOX_PORT=7894

# --- Security ---
# Comma-separated bearer tokens for the HTTP transport (stored/compared hashed)
# PROTOX_TOKENS=
# Per-tool ACL: JSON object token -> list of tool names, e.g. {"tok1":["image_info"]}
# PROTOX_TOOL_ACL=
# Policy preset: strict | network-egress | permissive-dev (see policies/*.yaml)
# PROTOX_POLICY_PRESET=network-egress
# Optional host allowlist for the HTTP adapter (comma-separated)
# PROTOX_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Server-side secrets for per-call dispatcher injection (never reach workers, INV-7)
# JSON object name -> value, e.g. {"MY_API_KEY":"..."}
# PROTOX_SECRETS=

# --- Nebius Token Factory (agent inference: judge / converter / repair) ---
# Without a key the server runs in degraded mode: 38 core tools live, agent features disabled (E-20)
# PROTOX_TF_API_KEY=
# PROTOX_TF_ENDPOINT=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1
# PROTOX_TF_JUDGE_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3-Ultra-550b-a55b
# PROTOX_TF_FAST_MODEL=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B
# PROTOX_TF_ESCALATION_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3-Ultra-550b-a55b

# --- Compute sizing (F-038) — override host-probed values ---
# PROTOX_CPUS=
# PROTOX_MEMORY=
# PROTOX_WORKER_POOL=
